      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a3c5fa04a8da67427803b3e|full_name}: I think a special case for AudioLink is a decent compromise. I get the reason for the prefix, but I think it's warranted here. I'm fine with this. \nI'm curious though, I thought this wouldn't be able to override anything declared as a property in the shader?  Isn't that how the regular SetGlobalTexture works? And if so, people would only be able to override some builtin textures, which I'd assume you could blacklist?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
